---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const page = {
  "brand": "iwatch",
  "title": "Privacy Policy · iWatch",
  "description": "How iWatch handles your library, iCloud sync, optional Trakt connection, and privacy choices.",
  "canonical": "https://tylerkeegan.com/iwatch/privacy/",
  "bodyClass": "theme-iwatch",
  "documentPage": true,
  "footerClass": "footer app-footer",
  "footerLinks": [
    {
      "href": "/iwatch/support/",
      "label": "Support"
    },
    {
      "href": "/iwatch/privacy/",
      "aria-current": "page",
      "label": "Privacy"
    },
    {
      "href": "/",
      "label": "Portfolio"
    }
  ],
  "footerSeparators": false
};
---
<SiteLayout {...page}>
<div class="hero-wrap"><section class="hero document-hero">
      <span class="tile"><img fetchpriority="high" width="88" height="88" decoding="async" src="/icons/iwatch-web.png" alt="iWatch app icon"></span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="meta">Last updated October 25, 2026</p>
    </section></div>
    <article class="document-copy" aria-label="Privacy Policy">
      <p>This policy explains how Tyler Keegan's iWatch app and its website handle information. iWatch helps you organize movies, TV shows, watchlists, episode progress, and viewing history. You do not need an iWatch account to use the app. Connecting a Trakt account is optional.</p>
      <h2>Your library and iCloud</h2>
      <p>The app stores your library on your device. This includes saved titles, watchlist entries, watched dates, episode progress, and information needed to keep your library in sync. Appearance and other preferences are also stored on your device, and downloaded artwork and responses may be cached.</p>
      <p>When iCloud is available, iWatch syncs library records through a private CloudKit database in your Apple account. Sync records can include Trakt account identifiers, pending library changes, and an app-generated device identifier used to coordinate changes across devices. This identifier is not an advertising identifier. The app does not send your library to an iWatch-operated server or publish it to other iWatch users. Apple's handling of iCloud information is described in its <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <h2>Optional Trakt connection</h2>
      <p>If you choose to connect Trakt in Settings, sign-in takes place through Trakt's authorization page. iWatch stores the resulting access and refresh tokens in your device's Keychain and uses an account identifier to associate sync with the correct Trakt account. iWatch does not ask you to enter your Trakt password into an iWatch form.</p>
      <p>Depending on your setup choice, iWatch imports your Trakt library or uploads your local watchlist and watched history. While connected, it exchanges title identifiers, watchlist changes, watched dates, and history entries with Trakt to keep your libraries in sync. This is part of the feature you enable, not advertising tracking. Trakt's retention, account privacy, and any sharing of activity on its service are governed by your Trakt settings and <a href="https://trakt.tv/privacy">Trakt's Privacy Policy</a>. Disconnecting iWatch does not delete information already stored in your Trakt account.</p>
      <h2>Search, artwork, and external services</h2>
      <p>iWatch requests movie, TV, cast, episode, and artwork information from The Movie Database (TMDB). Searches send the text you enter to TMDB; opening details or loading artwork sends the requested title, person, episode, or image identifiers. Provider discovery also sends a country or region code taken from your device's regional settings. The app does not request GPS location access for this feature.</p>
      <p>As with other internet requests, service providers receive technical connection information such as your IP address. Their own policies describe how they process and retain those requests; see <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/privacy-policy">TMDB's Privacy Policy</a>. Where-to-watch information is supplied through TMDB with JustWatch attribution. Opening a trailer, provider page, or cast member's external link takes you to another service, such as YouTube or JustWatch, whose policies apply when you visit it.</p>
      <h2>Notifications and permissions</h2>
      <p>Release reminders are optional. If you enable them, iWatch requests notification permission and schedules reminders on your device using titles and release dates from your library. You can change the reminder preferences in iWatch or notification permission in your device's Settings.</p>
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>The app does not include advertising SDKs or third-party analytics SDKs, and it does not use Apple's advertising identifier. Its library sync and catalog requests provide app features; they are not an iWatch advertising or cross-app tracking system. Apple and the external services described above may still receive technical or diagnostic information under their own policies.</p>
      <h2>Beta testing through TestFlight</h2>
      <p>Apple operates TestFlight and processes beta-testing information, including crash and usage data and feedback. Apple makes beta diagnostics and submitted feedback available to the app developer. Feedback can include screenshots and information you choose to send. Review <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/test-flight/">Apple's TestFlight privacy information</a> for details. Avoid including passwords or other sensitive information in feedback.</p>
      <h2>Your controls and deletion</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Disconnect Trakt:</strong> In Settings &gt; Trakt, choose Disconnect Trakt to stop this device's Trakt connection and remove its saved authorization. Your iWatch library remains on the device and in iCloud. Other connected devices and your Trakt account are separate.</li>
        <li><strong>Clear cached files:</strong> Settings &gt; Storage &amp; Data &gt; Clear Temporary Files removes downloaded artwork and network caches without removing your library.</li>
        <li><strong>Erase your iWatch library:</strong> Settings &gt; Storage &amp; Data &gt; Erase All App Data removes your iWatch library and preferences and sends the library deletion through iCloud. It also disconnects Trakt on this device. Keep the app installed and online until it confirms the iCloud update. The app reports if that update needs attention.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The app retains your library until you remove entries or erase it. Removing the app alone is not the same as erasing its iCloud data. Erasing iWatch data does not delete your Trakt account or its history; use Trakt's own controls for that. Apple and external providers control retention of information held in their services.</p>
      <h2>The iWatch website</h2>
      <p>This website stores your selected appearance preference in your browser's local storage. You can remove it by clearing this website's data. Loading the website sends technical request information, such as your IP address and browser details, to its hosting infrastructure. The website does not receive your in-app library or Trakt authorization. Links to TestFlight and other external sites are governed by those services' policies.</p>
      <h2>Contact and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>If you email support, your email address, message, and attachments are used to respond to your request and kept as needed to handle the correspondence. Do not send passwords, access tokens, or other private credentials, and hide personal information in screenshots. Send privacy questions or requests to access, correct, or delete support information to <a href="mailto:Tyler@Keegan.me">Tyler@Keegan.me</a>. For your library, use the in-app controls above; requests about information held by Apple or Trakt may also need to be addressed to those providers.</p>
      <h2>Age suitability</h2>
      <p>iWatch is a general movie and TV tracking app. Its catalog includes titles, descriptions, and artwork that may contain mature themes. Follow the app's regional App Store age rating and the age requirements of any external service you choose to use.</p>
      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>This policy will be updated when the app's features or information practices change. The date above identifies the latest revision.</p>
    </article>
</SiteLayout>
